 "title": "No row after the first is open, so knots across time cannot be read from the last growth event",
 "subject": "Networks of rings joined by shared contacts, read with the canonical knot test on their space-time law",
 "conclusion": "Every cell of these networks is read by exactly two cells, so every row after the first has a fixed parity and is not open. Reading knots from the last growth event therefore treats a determined row as open, and read natively from any later row the knots fail even without growth, so the loss under growth while running is real.",
